<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Contras</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1980s</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Contras were right-wing rebel groups that fought the Sandinista government of Nicaragua in the 1980s. Formed largely around former members of Anastasio Somoza's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-guard-panama">National Guard</a>, they were armed, trained and funded by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> and operated from camps in Honduras. Their war cost tens of thousands of lives, and secret US funding of the Contras led to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>–Contra affair.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/contras.jpg" alt="Contras" width="320" height="221" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Tiomono (talk) · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Contra_commandas_1987.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
